  "delivered": [
    "Removed unused pre-v3 classification, automatic plaintext-primary conversion and unsupported-upgrade fixtures/claims. Unsupported, unmarked, inconsistent and future primary data fail closed before writable setup.",
    "Normalized ordinary application/domain/storage/local-model modules and symbols through their actual callers without aliases. Retained only real compatibility/version identifiers.",
    "Fresh encrypted stores migrate privately, checkpoint, close and sync before no-clobber publication. Interrupted creation never publishes an ambiguous primary; recoverable artifacts prevent empty recreation.",
    "Append-only migrations32\u201334 normalize16 physical tables, five indexes and45 triggers without rebuilding rows or retaining alias views. Existing migrations0\u201332 remain byte-identical; all50 recreated guard/index definitions preserve normalized tokens and SQL strings.",
    "Pre-migration identity requires successful checksum-bound migration11 and, for the renamed layout,33. All16 physical table pairs follow their actual introduction/cutover versions; mixed/missing layouts refuse before writer mutation. Future-data diagnostics keep precedence.",
    "Eight reviewed-export-v1 record labels remain immutable; only their physical query targets change. Vectors, credentials, trust records and protected exclusions remain governed.",
    "Older supported-v3 backups inspect, stage, restore, promote and roll back across the physical rename. Promoted crash recovery reads retained WAL before writer setup. SQLCipher copies attach selected input read-only to an owned destination; original bytes and standalone sidecar absence are preserved.",
    "File URIs preserve relative/reserved paths and encode Windows drive/UNC forms. The existing URL owner handles generic path encoding; SQLite attachment policy stays in storage. External URL validation is unchanged.",
    "Retired company-key aliases and education/category scalar coercions are removed with explicit rejection, preserving files/runtime/filter/draft data. Canonical config, comments/help fields, duplicate-key errors, builder data and JSON Resume import remain supported.",
    "Workbench tests use a fixed reviewed date; production still uses the real clock and unchanged policy evidence. Minimum Gate4 dossier wiring has no confirmed development gap; broader runtime assurance remains R1.",
    "Removed startup plaintext-config secret extraction, clearing and migration-flag APIs. Both config constructors reject presence of all seven retired secret paths, including empty/null/mixed inputs, before decoding; file/runtime/vault bytes remain unchanged on refusal.",
    "Removed the per-secret OS compatibility reader/writer, lazy import and keyring-only service factory. Every runtime provider has a concrete vault repository; scheduler, notification and smoke owners use injected/current vault services. Missing rows return None; locked or unavailable storage returns sanitized errors.",
    "Explicit credential deletion, including both retired LinkedIn entries, remains available. Current database/vault-key OS protection, passphrase wrapping, user presence and stable identifiers remain unchanged. Isolated fixed-key tests never touch OS entries.",
    "Removed the newly unused credentials tempfile dev-dependency and only its lockfile edge; locked init completed with zero environment warnings and9 startup smoke tests. Updated current credential docs and security drift sensors without adding dependencies."
  ],
  "immutable_boundaries": [
    "Schema IDs, signing contexts, signature-covered pack keys, format versions, model/backend identities, export-v1 labels and applied migration bytes remain unchanged.",
    "Relational education graduation_year and its export remain current data. Fresh-install screening patterns, listed-pay/geography projections and secure-storage names remain required.",
    "No production signing enrollment, model/threshold change, package build, VM provisioning, credential read or publication occurred."
  ],
